# blackbox — Telemetry & Crash Autopsy
File: website/pulled/blackbox.oot

Source: openOODA/blackbox/docs/

## What it is

The agent-native execution flight recorder and crash autopsy engine. Tag v0.1.0.
Captures process telemetry, intercepts unhandled crash signals (SIGSEGV, SIGABRT, SIGBUS, SIGILL),
and diffs compiler intermediate representations across passes.

## Surface

Commands from `blackbox/docs/CLI.oot`:

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| blackbox autopsy [path] | Parse crash telemetry and output 1-turn diagnosis |
| blackbox diff <file.oo> | Diff AST across compiler passes (lex, ast, check, emit) |
| blackbox trace <file.oo> | Record and dump execution flight events |

## Architecture

Follows RFC 0005 layout:
- `record/`: In-memory flight data recorder and telemetry ring buffer.
- `autopsy/`: Crash analyzer, failure coordinate locator, and root cause classifier.
- `diff/`: AST pass diffing engine tailored for oodac debugging.
- `bridge/`: Process execution runner under explicit capability tokens.
- `cli/`: Terminal entry point for AI harnesses (antigravity-cli, devin, grok, mcode).
